/target

# The Python client's test server is its own cargo workspace, so the root
# `/target` rule does not reach its build output — 2.4k files and a 100 MB
# binary, which GitHub refuses. Same root cause as the rot recorded in
# 2026-09-13-python-grouped-join-and-a-rotted-testserver.md: being outside the
# root workspace means the root's rules do not apply to it.
clients/python/testserver/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Python client
clients/python/**/__pycache__/
clients/python/.pytest_cache/
clients/python/*.egg-info/
clients/python/src/*.egg-info/
